Created `src/unique.mjs`:

```js
/**
 * Removes duplicate values from an iterable, keeping first-seen order.
 *
 * Equality follows same-value-zero semantics (as used by `Set`), so
 * `NaN` is treated as equal to `NaN` and `0`/`-0` are considered equal.
 *
 * @template T
 * @param {Iterable<T>} values
 * @returns {T[]}
 */
export function unique(values) {
  if (values == null) {
    throw new TypeError('unique(values): values must be an iterable');
  }
  return [...new Set(values)];
}

export default unique;
```

Notes:
- Accepts any iterable (arrays, Sets, strings, generators) and returns a plain array.
- Order is preserved by construction: `Set` iteration order is insertion order of first occurrence.
